1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:04,050
Six homes across Southeast Asia, all under the same sun.

2
00:00:04,900 --> 00:00:08,540
Manila. Bangkok. Hanoi. Kuala Lumpur. Jakarta. Singapore.

3
00:00:19,100 --> 00:00:21,070
But someone is always watching.

4
00:00:21,100 --> 00:00:24,130
Your goal: let the sun in, and keep the watchers out.

5
00:00:24,100 --> 00:00:26,190
This is VaLora: Two Watchers.

6
00:00:27,100 --> 00:00:30,780
Our entry for the Meta VR Start Developer Competition.

7
00:00:31,400 --> 00:00:36,080
It's a single-player puzzle. The two watchers are the sun, and whoever looks in.

8
00:00:36,100 --> 00:00:39,310
Start on the globe. Pick a country, then enter VR.

9
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:43,940
Each one has its own house, its own sun path, and its own watchers.

10
00:00:45,300 --> 00:00:48,930
In the headset, stay seated. Use hands or controllers.

11
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:51,730
Point at Tiki the gecko, and pinch to start.

12
00:00:52,400 --> 00:00:56,510
Pinch a screen on the bamboo raft. Point it at the courtyard, and let go.

13
00:00:58,100 --> 00:01:00,060
Now the neighbour can't see your chair.

14
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:01,820
A short pinch turns a piece.

15
00:01:03,800 --> 00:01:09,500
Look around. Every watcher has a line of sight: the neighbour, the boats on the canal, and the sun.

16
00:01:11,200 --> 00:01:16,600
Pinch the sun and drag it across the sky. The shadows follow each city's own sun path.

17
00:01:16,900 --> 00:01:21,100
A spot is sunny when the sun can see it, and private when no one else can.

18
00:01:21,300 --> 00:01:25,920
Here's how you score. Each level has a few rules, and they start as not yet.

19
00:01:26,200 --> 00:01:30,700
This one has two watchers at once: the neighbour, and the riders in the lane.

20
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:34,390
A screen blocks the neighbour. A hedge blocks the riders.

21
00:01:35,400 --> 00:01:39,620
Every rule is done. Use the fewest pieces, and you earn three stars.

22
00:01:40,900 --> 00:01:44,110
Then press play to live the day. Every hour is checked.

23
00:01:47,900 --> 00:01:54,350
Prefer controllers? Point, and pull the trigger. In Hanoi, a hedge hides the table from the motorbikes.

24
00:01:55,800 --> 00:01:59,640
In Bangkok, a hedge hides the table from the long-tail boats.

25
00:02:03,700 --> 00:02:08,590
In Kuala Lumpur, condo towers look down. A tree's canopy hides the table.

26
00:02:11,600 --> 00:02:15,820
In Jakarta, a pergola keeps the table dry in the monsoon rain.

27
00:02:19,500 --> 00:02:23,940
In Singapore, a tree's canopy hides the pool from the high-rise next door.

28
00:02:27,250 --> 00:02:30,700
Eighteen levels, six capitals, all proven solvable.

29
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:33,640
Made by Aljabri Alam, in Singapore.

30
00:02:35,800 --> 00:02:38,810
VaLora. Let the sun in. Keep the watchers out.
